{
  "chapter_id": "05",
  "chapter_name": "入境通關",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": "05-001",
      "en": "What is the purpose of your visit?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "purpose",
          "kk": "/ˈpɜrpəs/",
          "zh": "目的"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "您來訪的目的是什麼？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "inspection",
        "question"
      ],
      "tips": "這是入境官員（immigration officer）最常問的問題之一。標準回答：Tourism（觀光）、Business（商務）、Visiting family（探親）。請簡潔明確地回答。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-002",
      "en": "I'm here for tourism.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "tourism",
          "kk": "/ˈtʊrɪzəm/",
          "zh": "旅遊"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "我來這裡觀光。",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "purpose",
        "response"
      ],
      "tips": "tourism 是「觀光、旅遊（活動）」，tourist 是「觀光客」。也可以說 I'm here on vacation（我來度假的）或 I'm here for sightseeing（我來觀光的）。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-003",
      "en": "How long are you planning to stay?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "planning",
          "kk": "/ˈplænɪŋ/",
          "zh": "規劃"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "您計劃停留多久？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "inspection",
        "question"
      ],
      "tips": "回答可說：Seven days（七天）、Two weeks（兩週）、About ten days（大約十天）。通常要與機票回程日期相符，建議事先確認。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-004",
      "en": "I'll be staying for ten days.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "staying",
          "kk": "/ˈsteɪɪŋ/",
          "zh": "停留"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "我將停留十天。",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "duration",
        "response"
      ],
      "tips": "回答停留時間時，加上 I'll be 更完整正式。也可說：I'm staying for ten days 或 My stay is ten days long。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-005",
      "en": "Where will you be staying?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "staying",
          "kk": "/ˈsteɪɪŋ/",
          "zh": "停留"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "您將住在哪裡？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "inspection",
        "question"
      ],
      "tips": "入境官員可能詢問住宿地點。請回答飯店名稱和城市，例如：At the Hilton Hotel in Tokyo（在東京希爾頓酒店）。出發前記下訂房確認信（booking confirmation）上的飯店地址。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-006",
      "en": "I'll be staying at the Grand Hyatt Hotel in New York.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "Grand Hyatt",
          "kk": "/ɡrænd haɪæt/",
          "zh": "君悅酒店"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "我將住在紐約的君悅大酒店。",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "accommodation",
        "response"
      ],
      "tips": "回答住宿地點時，提供飯店名稱和所在城市即可。如果你是到朋友或親戚家，可以說：I'll be staying with a friend in Los Angeles.（我將住在洛杉磯一位朋友家。）",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-007",
      "en": "Do you have anything to declare?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "declare",
          "kk": "/dɪˈklɛr/",
          "zh": "宣告"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "您有任何物品需要申報嗎？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "customs",
        "declaration"
      ],
      "tips": "declare 是「申報」。這個問題通常由海關人員（customs officer）詢問。如果有攜帶高額現金（通常超過 10,000 美元）、食品農產品或商業貨物，需要申報。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-008",
      "en": "Nothing to declare.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "declare",
          "kk": "/dɪˈklɛr/",
          "zh": "宣告"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "沒有需要申報的物品。",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "customs",
        "response"
      ],
      "tips": "這是最常見的回答。在機場通關時，通常分為「申報」（Goods to Declare）和「免申報」（Nothing to Declare）兩個通道，沒有申報物品請走綠色通道（green channel）。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-009",
      "en": "Please look into the camera for your photo and fingerprints.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "fingerprints",
          "kk": "/ˈfɪŋɡɚˌprɪnts/",
          "zh": "指紋"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "請看鏡頭，進行拍照和指紋採集。",
      "level": "B1",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "biometrics",
        "inspection"
      ],
      "tips": "許多國家（如美國、英國、日本）在入境時需要採集生物特徵（biometrics），包括臉部照片和十指指紋。這是標準程序，無需緊張，依指示操作即可。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-010",
      "en": "Is this your first time visiting the United States?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "visiting",
          "kk": "/ˈvɪzɪtɪŋ/",
          "zh": "來訪"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "這是您第一次來美國嗎？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "inspection",
        "question"
      ],
      "tips": "回答：Yes, it's my first time.（是的，這是我第一次。）或 No, I've been here before.（不，我以前來過。）保持輕鬆誠實地回答即可。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-011",
      "en": "Please fill out this arrival card.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "arrival card",
          "kk": "/əˈraɪvl kɑrd/",
          "zh": "到達卡"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "請填寫這張入境卡。",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "documents",
        "form"
      ],
      "tips": "arrival card（入境卡）是部分國家要求旅客填寫的表格，包含個人資料、旅行目的、住宿地址等。現在很多國家已改用電子入境申報，在飛機上或抵達前就可以線上填寫。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-012",
      "en": "My return flight is on the fifteenth of this month.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "return flight",
          "kk": "/rɪˈtɜrn flaɪt/",
          "zh": "回程班機"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "我的回程班機在這個月的十五號。",
      "level": "B1",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "flight",
        "response"
      ],
      "tips": "入境官員可能要求確認回程機票，以確保旅客不會逾期停留（overstay）。建議在手機裡儲存機票確認信或截圖，方便隨時出示。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-013",
      "en": "Could you please speak more slowly? My English is not perfect.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "slowly",
          "kk": "/ˈsloʊli/",
          "zh": "慢慢地"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "可以請您說慢一點嗎？我的英文不太好。",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "communication",
        "request"
      ],
      "tips": "遇到聽不懂的問題，主動請對方放慢語速是完全可以接受的做法。也可以說：Could you repeat that?（可以再說一遍嗎？）入境官員習慣與各國旅客溝通，會耐心配合。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-014",
      "en": "I have a connecting flight to Paris.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "connecting flight",
          "kk": "/kəˈnɛktɪŋ flaɪt/",
          "zh": "轉機航班"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "我有一班前往巴黎的轉機班機。",
      "level": "B1",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "transit",
        "flight"
      ],
      "tips": "過境旅客（transit passenger）有時走不同的通關通道（transit immigration）。若需要入境後再搭機，需要依正常入境程序辦理。入境前最好確認自己的行程需求。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-015",
      "en": "Welcome to Japan. Have a pleasant stay.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "pleasant",
          "kk": "/ˈplɛzənt/",
          "zh": "令人愉快的"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "歡迎來到日本，祝您旅途愉快。",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "immigration",
        "greeting",
        "welcome"
      ],
      "tips": "這是入境官員常用的歡迎語。pleasant 是「愉快的、令人高興的」，比 nice 更正式。可以回應：Thank you!（謝謝！）即可。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    }
  ],
